     "text": "CLINICAL SUMMARY - Carlson and Sons Medical Group\n\nPatient: Eric Boyer \nDOB: 05/06/1970 \nSex: M \nMRN: 394402\n\nEncounters:\n 2025-07-28 Alcohol use disorder (treated) BP 131/66 Wt 141\n 2024-07-01 Alcohol use disorder (treated) BP 127/68 Wt 129\n 2023-06-04 flu shot BP 127/65 Wt 128\n 2022-05-08 rash BP 137/69 Wt 128\n\nAssessment/Plan:\n• Alcohol use disorder (treated) (abstinent 3.1 yrs; treatment IOP; relapses 1) - controlled; meds: naltrexone 38D mg inj\n• Tobacco - cigar current 7/yr\n\nClinical Summary:\n\nEric Boyer, a 55-year-old male, presented for a follow-up appointment on July 28, 2025. The patient has a history of alcohol use disorder, which is currently in a controlled state, having been abstinent for 3.1 years. His treatment has included Intensive Outpatient Program (IOP), and he has experienced one relapse. \n\nDuring this visit, the patient reported no current issues with alcohol use and has been adherent to his treatment regimen, which includes naltrexone 380 mg injections. His blood pressure was recorded at 131/66 mmHg, and his weight was 141 pounds. \n\nOn July 1, 2024, Mr. Boyer came in for another follow-up visit regarding his alcohol use disorder. He again reported no issues with alcohol use and adherence to treatment. His blood pressure was 127/68 mmHg, and his weight was 129 pounds.\n\nThe patient received a flu shot on June 4, 2023. At that his blood pressure was 127/65 mmHg, and his weight was 128 pounds. This visit was routine and did not reveal any new issues.\n\nOn May 8, 2022, Mr. Boyer presented with a rash. His blood pressure was 137/69 mmHg, and his weight was 128 pounds. The rash was evaluated, and appropriate management was provided. \n\nSocial history reveals that Mr. Boyer currently uses cigars, smoking about seven times per year, a habit he has maintained since January 29, 2023. He has not attempted to quit and minimizes the disclosure of this habit.\n\nPhysical exams on the recent visits have been within normal limits, with no significant findings reported. Mr. Boyer’s family history is notable for his mother, who has Alzheimer’s disease, diagnosed at age 64, although she is still living.\n\nMr. Boyer is with his treatment plan and has not shown any signs of noncompliance with his medication or therapy. He is also reported to have no alcohol use beyond what is medically controlled and documented.\n\nAdditional routine content includes normal vital signs, including heart rate, respiratory rate, and temperature, which were all within normal ranges during the visits. Mr. Boyer reports no new complaints or issues"
